  "abstract": "Generative interpretation is the use of large language models to estimate contractual meaning, ordinary meaning, ambiguity, and gaps. The article develops the method through worked examples and examines its risks and institutional implications; it does not test judicial accuracy at scale or claim that models should replace judges.",
  "license": "https://rightsstatements.org/page/InC/1.0/",
